<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vítkovice ironworks</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vítkovice ironworks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrava">Ostrava</a> were founded in 1828 by Archduke Rudolf, archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a>, and were later owned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rothschild-family">Rothschild family</a>. Using <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> from the Ostrava basin, they became one of the largest iron and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> works in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg Monarchy</a> and the core of Ostrava's industrial growth. Nationalised after 1945, they remained a major Czechoslovak steel and engineering concern.</p></div>
